theory('Introduction to DP', 'Dynamic programming applies when subproblems overlap and a state captures every fact needed for future choices. Start with a recursive state definition, write choices and base cases, memoize by the complete state, then order a table so dependencies are computed first. Space compression is valid only after identifying which earlier rows are still needed. Existence uses OR, optimization min/max, counting sums. Do not confuse an uncomputed state with a legitimate zero or negative answer. Use separate visited flags or a sentinel outside the result range. Prove optimal substructure: replacing a chosen subproblem solution by a better one must improve the complete solution. The lessons below state the recurrence and provide executable tabulated/rolling implementations; they describe memoized alternatives where appropriate. Not every alternative has a separate code implementation.')
def dpadd(title,code,example,expected,contract,recurrence,cost,trace,edges='Validate nonnegative size/target parameters and respect the stated input domain. Java array dimensions must fit memory; recursion alternatives may exhaust the call stack.'):
    add(title,code,example,expected,contract,recurrence,cost,trace,edges,
        'Direct recursion follows the stated recurrence but may repeat overlapping states exponentially. Memoize the complete state to compute each once; tabulation in dependency order removes recursive frames. Rolling storage is valid only when all still-needed dependencies are retained. The provided code implements the method described above; alternative variants are explanations unless a separately named method is present.')

dpadd('Climbing stairs', '''    public static BigInteger solve(int n){if(n<0)throw new IllegalArgumentException();BigInteger a=BigInteger.ONE,b=BigInteger.ONE;for(int i=2;i<=n;i++){BigInteger next=a.add(b);a=b;b=next;}return b;}''','System.out.println(solve(5));','8',
    'Reach step n with jumps of one or two; n=0 has one empty way. Return exact count.', 'ways(i)=ways(i-1)+ways(i-2), because final jump is one of those two disjoint cases. Base ways(0)=ways(1)=1. Keep only the two preceding counts.', 'O(n) BigInteger additions, O(answer bits) retained storage.', 'ways: 1,1,2,3,5,8 for n=0..5.')
frog='''    public static long solve(int[] h,int k){if(k<1)throw new IllegalArgumentException();if(h.length==0)return 0;long[] d=new long[h.length];Arrays.fill(d,Long.MAX_VALUE);d[0]=0;for(int i=1;i<h.length;i++)for(int jump=1;jump<=k&&jump<=i;jump++)d[i]=Math.min(d[i],d[i-jump]+Math.abs((long)h[i]-h[i-jump]));return d[h.length-1];}'''
for title,k in [('Frog Jump',2),('Frog jump with K distances',3)]:
    dpadd(title,frog,'System.out.println(solve(new int[]{10,20,30,10},%d));'%k,'20' if k==2 else '0',
        'A frog starts at index zero and jumps 1..k forward indices. Cost is absolute height difference; return minimum total. Frog Jump uses k=2.',
        'dp[i]=min over j=1..k of dp[i-j]+abs(h[i]-h[i-j]). Every path has one last jump; minimizing each predecessor is safe by additive cost.', 'O(n*k) time, O(n) space.', 'k=2 permits 0->1->3 at cost 10+10=20; k=3 permits 0->3 at cost zero.', 'Widen height subtraction before abs; extreme int heights are supported.')
rob='''    static long linear(int[] a,int l,int r){long prev=0,before=0;for(int i=l;i<r;i++){if(a[i]<0)throw new IllegalArgumentException();long next=Math.max(prev,before+a[i]);before=prev;prev=next;}return prev;}
    public static long solve(int[] a){return linear(a,0,a.length);}'''
dpadd('Maximum sum of non adjacent elements',rob,'System.out.println(solve(new int[]{2,1,4,9}));','11',
    'Nonnegative array; maximize sum of a subset with no adjacent chosen indices. Empty subset allowed.', 'dp[i]=max(dp[i-1],a[i]+dp[i-2]): skip or take the last value. Keep two preceding states.', 'O(n) time, O(1) space.', 'Choose 2 and 9 for 11; choosing 4 would prevent adjacent 9.')
dpadd('House robber',rob.replace('return linear(a,0,a.length);','if(a.length==0)return 0;if(a.length==1)return a[0];return Math.max(linear(a,0,a.length-1),linear(a,1,a.length));'),
    'System.out.println(solve(new int[]{2,3,2}));','3', 'Circular house-robber variant: first and last are adjacent, nonnegative amounts.',
    'No valid solution takes both endpoints. Maximize the two linear cases excluding last or excluding first; together they cover every feasible selection.', 'O(n) time, O(1) space.', '[2,3,2]: endpoints cannot both be chosen; pick 3.', 'This sheet lesson uses the circular variant (House Robber II). The preceding nonadjacent lesson covers the ordinary linear version.')
dpadd("Ninja's training", '''    public static long solve(int[][] points){if(points.length==0)return 0;long[] prev=new long[3];for(int task=0;task<3;task++)prev[task]=points[0][task];for(int day=1;day<points.length;day++){long[] next=new long[3];for(int t=0;t<3;t++)next[t]=points[day][t]+Math.max(prev[(t+1)%3],prev[(t+2)%3]);prev=next;}return Math.max(prev[0],Math.max(prev[1],prev[2]));}''','System.out.println(solve(new int[][]{{10,40,70},{20,50,80},{30,60,90}}));','210',
    'Exactly one of three tasks daily; consecutive days cannot repeat the same task. Scores may be negative.', 'dp[day][task]=points[day][task]+max(prev[other task]). Starting from first-day scores ensures one task must be chosen even for negative values.', 'O(3*days) time, O(3) space.', '70 on day0,50 on day1,90 on day2 totals210.')
unique='''    public static BigInteger solve(int rows,int cols){if(rows<0||cols<0)throw new IllegalArgumentException();if(rows==0||cols==0)return BigInteger.ZERO;BigInteger[] d=new BigInteger[cols];Arrays.fill(d,BigInteger.ZERO);d[0]=BigInteger.ONE;for(int r=0;r<rows;r++)for(int c=1;c<cols;c++)d[c]=d[c].add(d[c-1]);return d[cols-1];}'''
dpadd('Grid unique paths',unique,'System.out.println(solve(3,7));','28','Move only right/down in an obstacle-free rows-by-cols grid; return exact path count.',
    'ways[r][c]=ways[r-1][c]+ways[r][c-1]. In a rolling row, d[c] is above and d[c-1] is already current-row left. Seed start with one.', 'O(R*C) BigInteger additions; O(C) BigIntegers.', 'A 3x7 grid needs two down and six right moves; choose their two down positions among eight gives28.')
dpadd('Unique paths II', '''    public static BigInteger solve(int[][] a){if(a.length==0||a[0].length==0)return BigInteger.ZERO;BigInteger[] d=new BigInteger[a[0].length];Arrays.fill(d,BigInteger.ZERO);d[0]=BigInteger.ONE;for(int[] row:a)for(int c=0;c<d.length;c++){if(row[c]==1)d[c]=BigInteger.ZERO;else if(c>0)d[c]=d[c].add(d[c-1]);}return d[d.length-1];}''','System.out.println(solve(new int[][]{{0,0,0},{0,1,0},{0,0,0}}));','2',
    '1 denotes obstacle,0 open; move right/down and return exact path count.', 'Blocked cells have zero ways. Others sum above and left using a rolling row. A blocked start correctly resets the initial one to zero.', 'O(R*C) BigInteger additions, O(C) retained values.', 'Center obstacle removes the four central routes; only the top/right boundary and left/bottom boundary routes remain.')
dpadd('Minimum Falling Path Sum', '''    public static long solve(int[][] a){if(a.length==0||a[0].length==0)return 0;long[] prev=new long[a[0].length];for(int c=0;c<prev.length;c++)prev[c]=a[0][c];for(int r=1;r<a.length;r++){long[] next=new long[prev.length];for(int c=0;c<prev.length;c++){long best=prev[c];if(c>0)best=Math.min(best,prev[c-1]);if(c+1<prev.length)best=Math.min(best,prev[c+1]);next[c]=best+a[r][c];}prev=next;}long best=Long.MAX_VALUE;for(long x:prev)best=Math.min(best,x);return best;}''','System.out.println(solve(new int[][]{{2,1,3},{6,5,4},{7,8,9}}));','13',
    'Start anywhere in row0; move down-left,down,down-right each row. Return minimum path sum.', 'dp[r][c]=a[r][c]+min of valid predecessor columns c-1,c,c+1. Only the previous row is needed.', 'O(R*C) time, O(C) space.', '1->5->7 sums13; 1->4->8 also sums13.')
dpadd('Triangle', '''    public static long solve(int[][] a){if(a.length==0)return 0;long[] d=new long[a[a.length-1].length];for(int i=0;i<d.length;i++)d[i]=a[a.length-1][i];for(int r=a.length-2;r>=0;r--)for(int c=0;c<a[r].length;c++)d[c]=a[r][c]+Math.min(d[c],d[c+1]);return d[0];}''','System.out.println(solve(new int[][]{{2},{3,4},{6,5,7},{4,1,8,3}}));','11',
    'Row r has r+1 entries. From (r,c) move to (r+1,c) or (r+1,c+1); minimize top-to-bottom sum.', 'Bottom-up dp[c]=value+min(down,diagonal). Updating left-to-right preserves the needed old d[c+1].', 'O(n²) time, O(n) space.', '2->3->5->1 gives11.', 'Validate triangular row lengths at the call site. Reverse-direction in-place updates would overwrite the next diagonal prematurely.')
dpadd('Cherry pickup II', '''    public static long solve(int[][] a){if(a.length==0||a[0].length==0)return 0;int cols=a[0].length;long[][] prev=new long[cols][cols];for(int x=0;x<cols;x++)for(int y=0;y<cols;y++)prev[x][y]=a[a.length-1][x]+(x==y?0L:a[a.length-1][y]);for(int r=a.length-2;r>=0;r--){long[][] next=new long[cols][cols];for(int x=0;x<cols;x++)for(int y=0;y<cols;y++){long best=Long.MIN_VALUE;for(int dx=-1;dx<=1;dx++)for(int dy=-1;dy<=1;dy++)if(x+dx>=0&&y+dy>=0&&x+dx<cols&&y+dy<cols)best=Math.max(best,prev[x+dx][y+dy]);next[x][y]=best+a[r][x]+(x==y?0L:a[r][y]);}prev=next;}return prev[0][cols-1];}''','System.out.println(solve(new int[][]{{3,1,1},{2,5,1},{1,5,5},{2,1,1}}));','24',
    'Two robots start at row0 columns0,last; each moves down with column delta -1,0,1. Collect both cells, once if coincident; maximize total.', 'State (row,col1,col2) captures both robot positions. Add current reward and maximize over nine next-position pairs; rolling 2D layers retain all dependencies.', 'O(R*C²*9) time, O(C²) space.', 'Robots collect both edge/frontier rewards while converging on high middle values; shared cells contribute once.')
dpadd('Count Square Submatrices with All Ones', '''    public static long solve(int[][] a){if(a.length==0)return 0;int[] prev=new int[a[0].length+1];long total=0;for(int[] row:a){int[] next=new int[prev.length];for(int c=1;c<next.length;c++)if(row[c-1]==1){next[c]=1+Math.min(prev[c],Math.min(prev[c-1],next[c-1]));total+=next[c];}prev=next;}return total;}''','System.out.println(solve(new int[][]{{1,1},{1,1}}));','5',
    'Count all-one axis-aligned square submatrices of a binary rectangular grid.', 'dp[r][c] is largest side ending at (r,c), one plus min(top,left,diagonal) for a one. Every side1..dp exists there, so add dp to total.', 'O(R*C) time, O(C) space.', 'Four unit squares plus one 2x2 square gives5.')

stock='''    public static long profit(int[] prices,int k,int fee,boolean cooldown){if(k<0||fee<0)throw new IllegalArgumentException();for(int p:prices)if(p<0)throw new IllegalArgumentException();k=Math.min(k,prices.length/2);long[][] next=new long[2][k+1],after=new long[2][k+1];for(int i=prices.length-1;i>=0;i--){long[][] cur=new long[2][k+1];for(int t=1;t<=k;t++){cur[0][t]=Math.max(next[0][t],-((long)prices[i])+next[1][t]);cur[1][t]=Math.max(next[1][t],prices[i]-(long)fee+(cooldown?after[0][t-1]:next[0][t-1]));}after=next;next=cur;}return next[0][k];}'''
stock_cases=[('Best time to buy and sell stock',1,0,False,'5'),('Best time to buy and sell stock II',3,0,False,'7'),('Best time to buy and sell stock III',2,0,False,'7'),('Best time to buy and sell stock IV',2,0,False,'7'),('Best time to buy and sell stock with transaction fees',3,2,False,'3'),('Best Time to Buy and Sell Stock with Cooldown',3,0,True,'5')]
for title,k,fee,cool,expected in stock_cases:
    dpadd(title,stock,'System.out.println(profit(new int[]{7,1,5,3,6,4},%d,%d,%s));'%(k,fee,str(cool).lower()),expected,
        'Nonnegative daily prices; at most k completed transactions, one share held at once. This lesson uses %s.'%('unlimited (pass n/2), fee '+str(fee)+', cooldown '+str(cool).lower() if k==3 else str(k)+' transactions; fee zero; no cooldown'),
        'State (day,holding,remainingSells). Not holding: max(skip,-price+holding tomorrow). Holding: max(skip,price-fee+notHolding after sell). A sell consumes one transaction; cooldown skips one subsequent day. Work backwards, retaining tomorrow and day-after states.',
        'O(n*k) time, O(k) rolling space; k is capped at floor(n/2). Unlimited variants can use constant-state O(n) algorithms instead.',
        'On [7,1,5,3,6,4], one trade1->6 yields5; two trades1->5 and3->6 yield7; charging fee2 per sell leaves3. Cooldown forbids buying immediately after selling.',
        'For III pass k=2; IV takes arbitrary k. II/fees/cooldown use k=n/2 for unlimited trades. Fees are charged at SELL only. Bounds assume final holding has no positive salvage value.')

subset_bool='''    static boolean[] reachable(int[] a,int target){if(target<0)throw new IllegalArgumentException();boolean[] d=new boolean[target+1];d[0]=true;for(int x:a){if(x<0)throw new IllegalArgumentException();for(int s=target;s>=x;s--)d[s]|=d[s-x];}return d;}
    public static boolean solve(int[] a,int target){return reachable(a,target)[target];}'''
dpadd('Subset sum equals to target',subset_bool,'System.out.println(solve(new int[]{1,2,3,4},6));','true',
    'Nonnegative values; decide whether a subset sums to target>=0. Empty subset allowed.', 'reachable[s] |= reachable[s-x] updates take/skip states. Descending sums ensure x is used at most once, because s-x still belongs to the prior item layer.', 'O(n*target) time, O(target) space.', 'Target6 is reached by2+4 or1+2+3.', 'Ascending sums would allow unlimited reuse; this is a 0/1 subset problem.')
dpadd('Partition equal subset sum',subset_bool.replace('public static boolean solve(int[] a,int target)','static boolean subset(int[] a,int target)')+'''\n    public static boolean solve(int[] a){long sum=0;for(int x:a){if(x<0)throw new IllegalArgumentException();sum+=x;}if(sum%2!=0)return false;if(sum/2>Integer.MAX_VALUE)throw new IllegalArgumentException("target too large");return subset(a,(int)(sum/2));}''','System.out.println(solve(new int[]{1,5,11,5}));','true',
    'Partition all nonnegative entries into two equal-sum subsets.', 'If total is odd impossible; otherwise one subset summing to total/2 leaves the complementary subset with exactly that same sum.', 'O(n*totalSum) time, O(totalSum) space.', '11 alone matches1+5+5=11.')
dpadd('Partition a set into two subsets with minimum absolute sum difference',subset_bool+'''\n    public static long difference(int[] a){long total=0;for(int x:a){if(x<0)throw new IllegalArgumentException();total+=x;}if(total/2>Integer.MAX_VALUE)throw new IllegalArgumentException();boolean[] d=reachable(a,(int)(total/2));for(int s=d.length-1;s>=0;s--)if(d[s])return total-2L*s;throw new IllegalStateException();}''','System.out.println(difference(new int[]{1,6,11,5}));','1',
    'Split nonnegative values minimizing absolute difference of the two subset sums.', 'Reachability up to half total suffices by complement symmetry. Largest reachable s<=total/2 minimizes total-2*s.', 'O(n*total) time, O(total) space.', 'Total23; subset11 or6+5 yields difference1.')
subset_count='''    static BigInteger count(int[] a,int target){if(target<0)return BigInteger.ZERO;BigInteger[] d=new BigInteger[target+1];Arrays.fill(d,BigInteger.ZERO);d[0]=BigInteger.ONE;for(int x:a){if(x<0)throw new IllegalArgumentException();for(int s=target;s>=x;s--)d[s]=d[s].add(d[s-x]);}return d[target];}
    public static BigInteger solve(int[] a,int target){return count(a,target);}'''
dpadd('Count subsets with sum K',subset_count,'System.out.println(solve(new int[]{0,0,1},1));','4',
    'Count POSITIONAL subsets of nonnegative entries summing to target; return exact BigInteger.', 'Counts add take and skip branches. Descending update prevents reuse; x=0 doubles every count because taking or skipping that zero are different positional choices.', 'O(n*target) BigInteger additions; O(target) stored values.', 'Each of two zeros is independently taken/skipped while1 is required, giving four.', 'Do not initialize dp[0] to one after every item; that would erase zero multiplicities.')
for title,sign in [('Count partitions with given difference',False),('Target sum',True)]:
    dpadd(title,subset_count.replace('public static BigInteger solve(int[] a,int target)','static BigInteger subsets(int[] a,int target)')+'''\n    public static BigInteger solve(int[] a,int difference){long sum=0;for(int x:a){if(x<0)throw new IllegalArgumentException();sum+=x;}long target=sum-(long)difference;if(target<0||target%2!=0||target/2>sum)return BigInteger.ZERO;if(target/2>Integer.MAX_VALUE)throw new IllegalArgumentException();return count(a,(int)(target/2));}''',
        'System.out.println(solve(new int[]{1,1,1,1,1},3));','5',
        'Count assignments of every nonnegative entry to two labeled sides with s1-s2=difference; Target sum interprets these as + and - signs.',
        's1+s2=total and s1-s2=d imply s2=(total-d)/2. If that is not an integer in [0,total], return zero; otherwise count positional subsets for the minus side.', 'O(n*derivedTarget) BigInteger additions and O(derivedTarget) values.', 'For five ones and difference3, choose any one as minus and four as plus: five assignments.', 'Zeros double assignments. Negative difference is allowed; labeled partitions/sign assignments are not unordered partitions.')
knapsack='''    public static long solve(int[] weight,int[] value,int capacity){if(capacity<0||weight.length!=value.length)throw new IllegalArgumentException();long[] d=new long[capacity+1];for(int i=0;i<weight.length;i++){if(weight[i]<=0)throw new IllegalArgumentException();LOOP d[c]=Math.max(d[c],value[i]+d[c-weight[i]]);}return d[capacity];}'''
for title,unbounded in [('0 and 1 Knapsack',False),('Unbounded knapsack',True)]:
    dpadd(title,knapsack.replace('LOOP','for(int c=weight[i];c<=capacity;c++)' if unbounded else 'for(int c=capacity;c>=weight[i];c--)'),
        'System.out.println(solve(new int[]{2,3},new int[]{4,5},6));','12' if unbounded else '9',
        'Positive integer weights; maximize total value within capacity. %s Empty selection allowed.'%('Each type can repeat.' if unbounded else 'Each input item can appear once.'),
        'dp[c]=max(skip,value[i]+dp[c-weight[i]]). %s'%('Ascending capacities read the current item layer, allowing reuse.' if unbounded else 'Descending capacities read the prior item layer, preventing reuse.'),
        'O(n*capacity) time, O(capacity) space.', 'Capacity6: 0/1 takes weights2+3 for value9; unlimited takes three weight2 items for12.', 'Zero weight with positive value makes unlimited optimum infinite; positive weights are required.')
dpadd('Rod cutting problem', '''    public static long solve(int[] prices){long[] d=new long[prices.length+1];Arrays.fill(d,Long.MIN_VALUE/4);d[0]=0;for(int length=1;length<=prices.length;length++)for(int cut=1;cut<=length;cut++)d[length]=Math.max(d[length],prices[cut-1]+d[length-cut]);return d[prices.length];}''','System.out.println(solve(new int[]{2,5,7,8,10}));','12',
    'prices[i] is sale value of length i+1. Cut and sell the WHOLE rod of length prices.length, pieces reusable.', 'dp[length]=max over first cut of price[cut-1]+dp[length-cut]. Smaller lengths are available first; exact length is required even for negative prices.', 'O(n²) time, O(n) space.', 'Length5 can split2+2+1 for5+5+2=12.')
dpadd('Minimum coins', '''    public static int solve(int[] coins,int target){if(target<0)throw new IllegalArgumentException();int[] d=new int[target+1];Arrays.fill(d,target+1);d[0]=0;for(int coin:coins){if(coin<=0)throw new IllegalArgumentException();for(int s=coin;s<=target;s++)d[s]=Math.min(d[s],1+d[s-coin]);}return d[target]>target?-1:d[target];}''','System.out.println(solve(new int[]{1,2,5},11));','3',
    'Unlimited positive denominations; minimize coins summing EXACTLY to target, -1 absent.', 'For each denomination, ascending sums allow reuse; minimize1+prior count. target+1 is an impossible-count sentinel because every usable coin is at least one.', 'O(n*target) time, O(target) space.', '11=5+5+1 uses three coins.', 'target must leave room for target+1 without int overflow and fit memory. Denomination duplicates do not affect minimum.')
dpadd('Coin change II', '''    public static BigInteger solve(int[] coins,int target){if(target<0)throw new IllegalArgumentException();Set<Integer> seen=new HashSet<>();BigInteger[] d=new BigInteger[target+1];Arrays.fill(d,BigInteger.ZERO);d[0]=BigInteger.ONE;for(int coin:coins){if(coin<=0||!seen.add(coin))throw new IllegalArgumentException("distinct positive denominations required");for(int s=coin;s<=target;s++)d[s]=d[s].add(d[s-coin]);}return d[target];}''','System.out.println(solve(new int[]{1,2,5},5));','4',
    'Count unordered combinations of unlimited DISTINCT positive coin denominations summing to target; exact BigInteger.', 'Process coin types outside and sums ascending inside, so each combination is counted once by its last processed type. Reversing loops would count ordered sequences.', 'O(coins*target) BigInteger additions; O(target) stored values.', 'Target5: five1s, three1s+2, one1+two2s, or one5 ->four.')
